This allows me to have a screen blanker that doesn't bother the port I
like to watch.

Whenever someone logs on, it disables the blanker.  When they log off,
it enables it.  Pretty simple.

The included script is used with the BeyondTheDark screen saver, but it
can be adapted to any other blanker with an ARexx port and ARexx commands
to disable and enable blanking.

To disable the blanker when someone is logging on, insert the following
text in your bbstext on line #22 BEFORE anything else on the line.

{#0PFiles:Blanker OFF}

To enable the blanker after they've logged off, insert the following text
at the end of the following lines in bbstext:  42,49,53,79-82 & 99

{#0PFiles:Blanker ON}

The above {'s are actually control-Q commands and remember to modify the
path to where you placed the "Blanker" script.
